- Story & Context: The city elders now tell the tale of the Great Inundation as a myth of rebirth, claiming that the piano melody heard on that first night was the sound of the ocean claiming its bride. Old Man Javi, the only survivor of that rooftop rave, sits by the edge of the water everyday, tapping a rhythm on a rusted oil drum that mimics the original, legendary composition. "We are only guests of the gravity," he croons to the seagulls, his voice echoing off the skyscraper canyons like a forgotten broadcast signal from a time when the sky was still reachable.
